    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but that \"defiance\" you're talking about... it feels so exhausting. why would i want to author a play that i know is going to end in nothing? it feels like i'm just prolonging a process that's already essentially over. if the pattern is just temporary and meaningless, then the only logical thing is to stop fighting the entropy. isn't there a certain kind of peace in just accepting that the struggle is unnecessary?",
